  <h2 id="glossary">Foundations glossary</h2>

  <dl class="terms">
    <dt>Foundry resource</dt>
    <dd>The single Azure resource that scopes models, agents, tools, RBAC, networking and policy.</dd>
    <dt>Foundry project</dt>
    <dd>A child resource of the Foundry resource; the workspace where agents, files, vector stores and evaluations live.</dd>
    <dt>Deployment</dt>
    <dd>A named, callable instance of a model in your resource. The name you pass as <code>model=</code>.</dd>
    <dt>Responses API</dt>
    <dd>The current inference and agent API (Agents v2). Replaces the Assistants API.</dd>
    <dt>Conversation</dt>
    <dd>Server-side multi-turn state. Replaces "thread". Holds <em>items</em> (replacing "messages").</dd>
    <dt>Agent version</dt>
    <dd>An immutable snapshot of an agent definition. Replaces "assistant"; enables rollback and comparison.</dd>
    <dt>Toolbox</dt>
    <dd>A curated, versioned collection of tools exposed through one managed MCP-compatible endpoint, reusable across agents and frameworks.</dd>
    <dt>Guardrail</dt>
    <dd>A named collection of <em>controls</em>; each control pairs a risk, an intervention point and an action.</dd>
    <dt>Foundry IQ</dt>
    <dd>The managed knowledge layer built on Azure AI Search that turns enterprise content into reusable, permission-aware knowledge bases for agents.</dd>
    <dt>PTU</dt>
    <dd>Provisioned Throughput Unit — the unit of reserved model capacity for provisioned deployment types.</dd>
    <dt>Foundry Tools</dt>
    <dd>The renamed Azure AI Services: Content Understanding, Language, Speech, Translator, Vision, Content Safety.</dd>
  </dl>

